[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928093953","pull_request_review_id":2571650473,"id":1928093953,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5y7GEB","diff_hunk":"@@ -2510,7 +2510,7 @@ bool RendererSceneCull::_light_instance_update_shadow(Instance *p_instance, cons\n \t\t\t\t}\n \n \t\t\t\treal_t radius = RSG::light_storage->light_get_param(p_instance->base, RS::LIGHT_PARAM_RANGE);\n-\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.005f, radius);\n+\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.025f, radius);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This will work at the default radius, but its going to break once the radius changes isn't it?","created_at":"2025-01-24T05:07:41Z","updated_at":"2025-01-24T05:07:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928093953","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928093953"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928093953"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928093953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2513,"original_line":2513,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928314744","pull_request_review_id":2572010567,"id":1928314744,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5y7794","diff_hunk":"@@ -2510,7 +2510,7 @@ bool RendererSceneCull::_light_instance_update_shadow(Instance *p_instance, cons\n \t\t\t\t}\n \n \t\t\t\treal_t radius = RSG::light_storage->light_get_param(p_instance->base, RS::LIGHT_PARAM_RANGE);\n-\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.005f, radius);\n+\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.025f, radius);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It works with all radiuses, and it's not related to the value of the constant (this adjustment is only meant to align the new default behavior with the previous one).\r\n\r\nThe reason why it works irrespective of the range is different for Omnis and Spotlights : \r\n\r\n#### For Omnis\r\nBias is applied in **view space** as a constant  z-offset :\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl#L435-L437\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl#L543\r\n\r\nThis is because `omni_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix` is **not a projection matrix** as its name may suggest but [the light's modelview matrix](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.cpp#L982-L984).\r\n\r\n:point_right: None of the above depend on the shadow *projection* matrix, therefore the bias does not depend on the range.\r\n\r\n#### For Spotlights\r\nBias is applied in **clip space**, now as a constant z-offset (see diff of scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl).\r\n\r\nThis is because unlike Omnis, `spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix` *is* the [shadow projection matrix](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.cpp#L1004-L1006).\r\n\r\nBut because znear is a small constant since #100319, clip space z coordinate does not depend on znear, nor on zfar as long as it is significantly larger than znear (consequence of `proj[2][2] = -(f+n)/(f-n)` converging to -1 when `n` is small). And if any use case would require the light range to be as low as 0.025 and shadows are on, visual artifacts would be very very small.\r\n\r\n:point_right: the bias is constant irrespective of the range.","created_at":"2025-01-24T08:28:14Z","updated_at":"2025-01-24T13:38:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928314744","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928314744"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928314744"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928314744/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2513,"original_line":2513,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1928093953,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928636949","pull_request_review_id":2572576210,"id":1928636949,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5y9KoV","diff_hunk":"@@ -733,7 +733,7 @@ void light_process_spot(uint idx, vec3 vertex, vec3 eye_vec, vec3 normal, vec3 v\n \t\tvec4 v = vec4(vertex + normal_bias, 1.0);\n \n \t\tvec4 splane = (spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix * v);\n-\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias / (light_length * spot_lights.data[idx].inv_radius);\n+\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias;","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The other comment by @clayjohn now makes me wonder if I should still keep the scaling by `light_length` : \r\n```glsl\r\nsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias / light_length\r\n```\r\n\r\nWithout it shadows might now be distorted close to the light's range.\r\nWill make a test with some geometry more complex than a box.","created_at":"2025-01-24T12:52:20Z","updated_at":"2025-01-24T12:52:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928636949","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928636949"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928636949"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928636949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":736,"original_line":736,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928666396","pull_request_review_id":2572626346,"id":1928666396,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5y9R0c","diff_hunk":"@@ -733,7 +733,7 @@ void light_process_spot(uint idx, vec3 vertex, vec3 eye_vec, vec3 normal, vec3 v\n \t\tvec4 v = vec4(vertex + normal_bias, 1.0);\n \n \t\tvec4 splane = (spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix * v);\n-\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias / (light_length * spot_lights.data[idx].inv_radius);\n+\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias;","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Did a few tests and restoring `light_length` didn't change anything visible on the shape of the shadow, but reintroduced a lot of self-shadowing as soon as the fragment is farther apart from the spotlight than ~40 units.\r\nThis is not a surprise in the end as dividing by `light_length` essentially cancels out the bias effect for far away fragments.\r\nI'm going to keep it as is for now, unless other contributors see something I would have overlooked.","created_at":"2025-01-24T13:17:59Z","updated_at":"2025-01-24T13:17:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928666396","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928666396"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1928666396"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1928666396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":736,"original_line":736,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1928636949,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1941796780","pull_request_review_id":2593879496,"id":1941796780,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5zvXes","diff_hunk":"@@ -733,7 +733,7 @@ void light_process_spot(uint idx, vec3 vertex, vec3 eye_vec, vec3 normal, vec3 v\n \t\tvec4 v = vec4(vertex + normal_bias, 1.0);\n \n \t\tvec4 splane = (spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix * v);\n-\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias / (light_length * spot_lights.data[idx].inv_radius);\n+\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias;","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I don't think this makes sense. Clip space is not a linear space. So using a fixed bias is bound to cause issues at one end of the space or the other. \r\n\r\nI think we should go forward with this PR without this change and then re-evaluate for 4.5 is this is worth making. At this point I think its best to just fix the regression","created_at":"2025-02-04T19:46:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-04T20:21:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1941796780","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1941796780"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1941796780"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1941796780/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":736,"original_line":736,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1928636949,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1941804254","pull_request_review_id":2593891652,"id":1941804254,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5zvZTe","diff_hunk":"@@ -2510,7 +2510,7 @@ bool RendererSceneCull::_light_instance_update_shadow(Instance *p_instance, cons\n \t\t\t\t}\n \n \t\t\t\treal_t radius = RSG::light_storage->light_get_param(p_instance->base, RS::LIGHT_PARAM_RANGE);\n-\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.005f, radius);\n+\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.025f, radius);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Makes sense. I'm still a bit skeptical, but at least now the behaviour for lights at and smaller than the default range is the same as it was in 4.3. \r\n\r\nAs Calinou highlights, this change maintains the high risk of self-shadowing for high ranges (since there will be a noticeable precision loss when increasing the range much higher than the default","created_at":"2025-02-04T19:52:17Z","updated_at":"2025-02-04T20:21:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1941804254","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1941804254"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1941804254"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1941804254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2513,"original_line":2513,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1928093953,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1942560214","pull_request_review_id":2595163314,"id":1942560214,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5zyR3W","diff_hunk":"@@ -733,7 +733,7 @@ void light_process_spot(uint idx, vec3 vertex, vec3 eye_vec, vec3 normal, vec3 v\n \t\tvec4 v = vec4(vertex + normal_bias, 1.0);\n \n \t\tvec4 splane = (spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix * v);\n-\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias / (light_length * spot_lights.data[idx].inv_radius);\n+\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias;","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Both this change and the other are necessary to fix the regression :\r\n- the other one ensures peter-panning is as small as before with default settings\r\n- this change makes peter-panning constant no matter the light range\r\n\r\nAnd for clarity:\r\nClip space *is* linear - it's just a scaled / skewed / translated version of the view space.\r\nYou maybe meant *ndc* space which indeed *is not* because of perspective division.\r\n\r\nApplying a fixed bias in clip space (or view space) is the way to go.\r\nPrior to this PR, the bias was scaled because the near plane was dynamically adjusted based on the light's range.\r\nOne unit in clip space represents different depths depending on the near plane setting. The scaling factor was intended to compensate for this, ensuring consistent peter-panning regardless of the light's range.\r\n\r\nNow the near plane is fixed since #100319, one unit in clip space represents always the same depth and there is nothing to compensate for anymore - bias can (and must) now be applied as usual as a constant offset. I missed that in #100319 and it contributed to the regression.","created_at":"2025-02-05T09:52:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-05T11:14:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1942560214","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1942560214"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1942560214"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1942560214/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":736,"original_line":736,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1928636949,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1942632644","pull_request_review_id":2595279613,"id":1942632644,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5zyjjE","diff_hunk":"@@ -2510,7 +2510,7 @@ bool RendererSceneCull::_light_instance_update_shadow(Instance *p_instance, cons\n \t\t\t\t}\n \n \t\t\t\treal_t radius = RSG::light_storage->light_get_param(p_instance->base, RS::LIGHT_PARAM_RANGE);\n-\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.005f, radius);\n+\t\t\t\treal_t z_near = MIN(0.025f, radius);","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Happy to clarify or do anything more to make you fully comfortable with it.\r\n\r\n> this change maintains the high risk of self-shadowing for high ranges\r\n\r\nSelf shadowing happens with large ranges *only on far away geometry* : now we use reverse-z precision is much less of a problem even with very small z-near.\r\n\r\nThis means there should not be any visual change with shadows on reasonably closeby geometry, even with large light ranges.","created_at":"2025-02-05T10:38:12Z","updated_at":"2025-02-05T11:16:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1942632644","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1942632644"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101952#discussion_r1942632644"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101952"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1942632644/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":2513,"original_line":2513,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1928093953,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1945627619","pull_request_review_id":2600276733,"id":1945627619,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5z9-vj","diff_hunk":"@@ -733,7 +733,7 @@ void light_process_spot(uint idx, vec3 vertex, vec3 eye_vec, vec3 normal, vec3 v\n \t\tvec4 v = vec4(vertex + normal_bias, 1.0);\n \n \t\tvec4 splane = (spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_matrix * v);\n-\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias / (light_length * spot_lights.data[idx].inv_radius);\n+\t\tsplane.z += spot_lights.data[idx].shadow_bias;","path":"servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/scene_forward_lights_inc.glsl","commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","original_commit_id":"d08ff57148c42b63e74adb669f6937d35fde1f6e","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> And for clarity:\r\n> Clip space is linear - it's just a scaled / skewed / translated version of the view space.\r\n> You maybe meant ndc space which indeed is not because of perspective division.\r\n\r\nThat's right, my mistake. \r\n\r\nThis should be fine then. I tested it locally and it appears to be at least as good as the situation in 4.3. So let's go ahead with this and see if anything else breaks. ","created_at":"2025-02-06T23:51:58Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T23:51:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pu